From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8010-7: Give the iPhone 7 battery
 temperature limits

The SN2400 charger follows the battery temperature against the monitored
battery's limits. The iPhone 7 and 7 Plus use the same charger driver,
and their gauge reports the battery temperature too, but their battery
gave no limits, so the guard did nothing there. Give it the A9 iPhones'
limits: off outside 0..45 C, reduced outside 10..40 C. They are generic
Li-ion charging limits, not values of one cell, and sit inside the JEITA
charging guideline; say so next to both.

Untested on the iPhone 7.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi |  5 ++++-
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi      | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
index 4bb2c49..a5623d6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
@@ -101,7 +101,10 @@
 		/*
 		 * The charger's input follows the battery temperature: off
 		 * outside 0..45 C, reduced outside 10..40 C. The ADT gives no
-		 * limits; these are the usual ones for Li-ion cells.
+		 * limits; these are the usual ones for Li-ion cells, inside
+		 * the JEITA charging guideline (no charge below 0 C, reduced
+		 * current from 0 to 10 C, normal from 10 to 45 C), with 40 to
+		 * 45 C also reduced as a margin.
 		 */
 		operating-range-celsius = <0 45>;
 		alert-celsius = <10 40>;
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi
index ac86a47..68aaf91 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi
@@ -150,6 +150,16 @@
 	battery_info: battery {
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
 		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1950000>;
+		/*
+		 * The charger's input follows the battery temperature: off
+		 * outside 0..45 C, reduced outside 10..40 C. The ADT gives no
+		 * limits; these are the usual ones for Li-ion cells, inside
+		 * the JEITA charging guideline (no charge below 0 C, reduced
+		 * current from 0 to 10 C, normal from 10 to 45 C), with 40 to
+		 * 45 C also reduced as a margin.
+		 */
+		operating-range-celsius = <0 45>;
+		alert-celsius = <10 40>;
 	};
 
 	wlan_vdd: regulator-wlan-vdd {
